and tied them with a rope and tortured them night and day so that he might
interrogate them about their involvement (amr). When the Apostle of God,
may God bless him and his family, knew of his presence at Badr, he
beseeched God that his affair would be sufficient (to destroy) him. He said:
"O God, be sufficient on my behalf (to destroy) Nawfal b. Khuwaylid."
Thus, the Commander of the faithful, peace be on him, killed him.

